% --- Title Information ---
\title{\textbf{Interactive Multi-Objective Optimization for Balancing Accuracy, Fairness, and Energy Efficiency in AI Models}}
\author{Sajid Ahmed Siddiqui}
\date{April 1st, 2026}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
Machine learning systems are increasingly deployed in high-stakes domains, raising critical concerns regarding fairness, bias, and sustainability. Models optimized solely for predictive accuracy often exhibit discriminatory behavior toward protected groups and incur significant computational and energy costs. Recent research highlights the need for multi-objective optimization (MOO) frameworks that explicitly balance competing objectives such as accuracy, fairness, and energy consumption.

This study proposes an interactive, in-processing multi-objective optimization techniques that integrates Interactive Training with the Non-dominated Sorting Genetic Algorithm II (NSGA-II). The framework jointly optimizes predictive accuracy, group fairness loss, individual fairness loss, and energy consumption. Fairness and bias are evaluated using the Adult Census Income and COMPAS datasets, while energy consumption is analyzed using the LCBench benchmark from the OpenML CC-18 suite. Interactive Training enables real-time human or agent intervention during optimization, allowing dynamic exploration of ethical and computational trade-offs. The proposed approach aims to improve transparency, adaptability, and sustainability in fairness-aware machine learning systems.
\end{abstract}

