\subsection{Modular Implementation and Decoupling}

\subsubsection{Data Handling Refactor: data\_loader.py and DataLoader Mechanics}
The data operations were decoupled into a dedicated pipeline using PyTorch \texttt{Dataset} and \texttt{DataLoader} classes, enabling Mini-Batch Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) and providing granular ``pulse points'' for interactivity.

\subsection{Dataset Characteristics and Preprocessing Pipelines}
Two disparate dataset paradigms were implemented to test the engine's limits:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Tabular Data (Adult Census):} Processed using \texttt{StandardScaler} and \texttt{OneHotEncoder}. Sensitive attribute 'Sex' is isolated for fairness calculation.
    \item \textbf{Vision Data (SyntheticVisionDataset):} A custom generator streaming $3 \times 64 \times 64$ tensors to simulate heavy Convolutional processing loops and hardware stress.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Model Diversity and Algorithmic Complexity}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Logistic Regression (Linear):} A single fully-connected (\texttt{nn.Linear}) layer as a baseline.
    \item \textbf{Deep Neural Networks (Non-Linear):} A multi-layer perceptron (MLP) with ReLU activations and Dropout (0.2).
    \item \textbf{ResNet-18 (Vision):} A deep CNN containing complex skip-connections, overriding the final layer for binary sigmoid classification.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{The Multi-Objective Loss Function Formulation}
The mathematical epicenter enabling the entire engine is the unified scalarization penalty:
\begin{equation}
    \text{Loss}_{total} = (w_{acc} \times L_{BCE}) + (w_{fair} \times (\mu_{priv} - \mu_{unpriv})^2) + (w_{nrg} \times \sum_{i}||\theta_i||_2)
\end{equation}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Accuracy Penalty:} Standard Binary Cross-Entropy loss.
    \item \textbf{Fairness Penalty:} Uses the squared difference in means of probability activations for privileged vs unprivileged groups.
    \item \textbf{Energy Regularization:} Employs $L_2$ parameter density constraints to force sparsity and reduce computational footprints.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Interactivity Implementation Details}
The system circumvents the ``deadlock'' dilemma by ensuring the \texttt{time.sleep(0.5)} block explicitly wraps the \texttt{process\_queues()} function. Even while paused, the thread actively listens for incoming JSON payloads from the Orchestrator.

\section{Results and Analysis}

\subsection{Comparative Model Performance}
Tests demonstrated robust multi-threading. The UI tracked Adult Income DNN and ResNet-18 instances simultaneously without observable frame lags. Linear models achieved stability in seconds, while ResNet-18 required extensive epochs to effectively organize convolutional filters.

\subsection{Fairness Trade-off Analysis in Active Environments}
Manual user interactions confirmed the theoretical trade-off theorems:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Baseline State:} High bias observed when $w_{fairness} = 0$.
    \item \textbf{Intervention Velocity:} Tuning the slider mid-training at Epoch 10 triggered an immediate drop in bias on the next batch iteration. 
    \item \textbf{Accuracy Degradation:} Reducing bias forced a proportionate degradation in Accuracy, proving the MOO system works as intended.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Energy Consumption Profiling}
Hardware profiling revealed sharp differences in demands:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Linear Trace:} Minimal deviation from baseline system idle states.
    \item \textbf{Vision Spikes:} ResNet-18 caused immediate estimated power demand spikes (approximating 100W+ TDP), highlighting the environmental costs of visual classification.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Interactivity Evaluation: Verifying the ``Change Since Tuning''}
A ``delta tracking'' system was authored for the UI. Upon injection of new parameters, the system registers a baseline and renders continuous colored $\Delta$ deviation metrics. This verified that specific $w_{fairness}$ interventions improved parity metrics by quantifiable amounts (e.g., $+0.3201\%$) since the moment of injection.

\subsection{User Interface Optimization and Reporting Efficacy}
Converting reporting from 'per-epoch' to 'per-iteration' significantly enhanced interactivity. Automated CSV generation empowered retrospective analysis of the accuracy vs fairness trajectory.

\section{Conclusion and Recommendations}

\subsection{Summary of Analytical Findings}
This research successfully deployed a Triple-Tier architecture isolating web-rendering from PyTorch mechanics. It proved that Operators can execute dynamic trade-off alterations across model complexities ranging from linear matrices to convolutional abstractions without inducing deadlocks.

\subsection{Critical Analysis of Interactive Training Paradigms}
Dynamic interactivity revolutionizes algorithmic development, allowing researchers to monitor demographic output paths and combat emerging prejudices by pulling an external slider.

\subsection{Limitations of the Current Technical Scope}
Energy profiling relies on software heuristics and static TDP assumptions rather than physical kernel-level power meters. Fairness constraints were simplified to binary Boolean groups, omitting complex intersectional definitions.

\subsection{Recommendations for Future Work}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Hardware Integrations:} Link with NVML APIs for raw silicon watt metrics.
    \item \textbf{NLP Scope:} Extend the framework to process Transformer components (e.g., DistilBERT) to combat toxic linguistic association.
    \item \textbf{Intersectional Parity:} Support multi-class intersectional constraints encompassing age, race, and gender simultaneously.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Final Concluding Remarks}
As AI architectures consume unparalleled energy to dictate sociological resolutions, retrospective tracking is insufficient. Live optimization interactivity merges static constraints with human oversight, ensuring a future of verifiable demographic equity and network efficiency.

